  ],
  "details": "",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The unlocated Babylonian city is mentioned in cuneiform documents of the second and first millennia B.C. Information provided the texts seem to indicate that Ba\u1e63, whose name might derive from the Akkadian word for sand, might be located somewhere near Sippar, perhaps close to the Euphrates River.",
